> 1. Is it worth doing Sokoban?  I could always bless magic lamp and
> wish up SDSM, and then I'd have reflection and a BoH.

I'd go ahead and do Sokoban, for the chance at a "oR.  It's also worth
doing for the extra food and wands, and more gold for donating.  And
heck, at level 11, you need more XP anyway.

> 2. Is it worth entering Sokoban and reverse-genociding nurses?  ie -
> do mid-game wizards have hitpoint issues?

Hard for me to say.  I recently ascended a wizard, but he had
ridiculous stats (1800HP, 2000Pw), due to being somewhat extinctionist.
In general, I'd say HP problems depends wholly upon playing style.
If you take your time, you'll never have problems.  If you're feeling
insecure, make a point of stockpiling !oEH and !oFH, and when you've
reached the castle, bless them and chug them all.

Your HP is currently much lower than I'd be comfortable with in the
castle.  I tend to wait until I can zap and bash monsters without
bothering to evade, much like a combat wombat.  You'd be spent after
about 14 magic missiles, though, and 72 HP wouldn't last long.

> 3. How close am I to being ready for the quest?  And what am I to
> expect?  Any tips?

The quest is a piece of cake.  Mostly bats, and several falling rock
traps.  The Dark One won't be very threatening as long as you have
your CoMR.  He might take a while to kill with that +0 Magicbane,
however.  Try to enchant it to +2 (optimum).  He resists magic as
well, note.

> 4. Do wizards normally do the castle or the quest first?  (Medusa
> won't be a problem - I have a pickaxe, a towel, and a mirror)

Quest, I'd say.  It's easier than the castle IMO, and the Eye is a
wonderful, wonderful artifact.

> 5. Are there any glaring gaps in my equipment?

So far, SDSM would be nice.  You should also be collecting elven
daggers to enchant and throw.  I guess I can assume you have a blessed
unicorn horn, luckstone, etc. by now.

Spellwise, remove curse and FoD would be nice to have.

I would've hunted down a fairly nice studded leather by now.

You may want an oilskin sack (or normal sack if necessary) in which to
keep your BoH, so that it won't become un-blessed.

